One can reduce water and electricity consumption in daily life by following several steps: 

1. Limiting water usage, e.g. refraining from bathing and washing clothes every day or installing low-flow showerheads to reduce water usage;
2. Unplugging electrical appliances which are not in use or using power strips to turn off multiple devices at once; 
3. Utilizing natural light as much as possible, e.g. turning the lights off while reading books;  4.. Using energy-efficient appliances that will save on power consumption; 
5. Installing temperature regulation systems to save money on cooling/heating bills during peak seasons
